        "original_id": "4d2789ef-202a-5a18-b1be-ae20d8c5ff13",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Flexible-fuel vehicles, bi-fuel vehicles, hydrogen vehicles\n- Concepts: Fuel storage, onboard fuel, motive power, CNG, LPG, hydrogen\n\nFacts:\n- Flexible-fuel vehicles are different from bi-fuel vehicles.\n- Bi-fuel vehicles store two fuels in separate tanks and run the engine on one fuel at a time.\n- Examples of fuels used in bi-fuel vehicles include compressed natural gas (CNG), liquefied petroleum gas (LPG), and hydrogen.\n- A hydrogen vehicle is a vehicle that uses hydrogen as its onboard fuel for motive power.",
